  ('retrovirus', 'retrovírus', 'A type of virus that stores its genetic information as RNA and uses an enzyme called reverse transcriptase to convert its RNA into DNA, which then integrates into the host cell''s genome.', 'HIV is a well-known retrovirus that attacks the immune system.', 'C1', 'noun', 'science', 44403),
