  ('thallium', 'tálio', 'A soft, grey, malleable metallic element that resembles tin but discolors on exposure to air; it is highly toxic and used in rodent and insect poisons; occurs in zinc blende and some iron ores.', 'Thallium is a heavy metal that can be found in trace amounts in the earth''s crust.', 'C2', 'noun', 'science', 46272),
