  ('gizzard', 'moela', 'A thick-walled, muscular pouch located in the digestive tract of birds, reptiles, and some other animals, which grinds food, often with the aid of ingested grit or stones.', 'Many birds swallow small pebbles to help their gizzard break down seeds and insects.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 47613),
