  ('periwinkle', 'pervinca', 'A type of plant, often with trailing stems and blue flowers, that is known to be poisonous.', 'The garden was full of periwinkle, its blue flowers spreading across the ground.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48403),
  ('rasp', 'raspar', 'To scrape or rub with a coarse file or similar tool, often used for shaping wood or metal.', 'He rasped the rough edges of the wooden plank.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 48408),
  ('hallow', 'santificar', 'To set apart as holy; to consecrate or venerate.', 'The priest hallowed the ground for the new church.', 'C1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 48411),
  ('quieten', 'acalmar-se', 'To become less noisy or to make less noise.', 'The children finally quietened down after their mother spoke.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 48422),
  ('amply', 'amplamente', 'In a way that is enough or more than enough; abundantly.', 'The evidence amply supports the conclusion.', 'C1', 'adverb', 'general-vocabulary', 48424),
  ('frivolity', 'frivolidade', 'Behavior or activity that is not serious, sensible, or important; lightheartedness.', 'The meeting was interrupted by moments of frivolity.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48433),
  ('transplantation', 'transplantação', 'The act of moving something from one place to another.', 'The transplantation of the ancient tree to the botanical garden was carefully planned.', 'B2', 'noun', 'health', 48442),
  ('oratory', 'oratória', 'The art or practice of delivering formal speeches to an audience, often characterized by rhetorical skill and sometimes perceived as pompous.', 'The senator''s oratory captivated the entire chamber.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48443),
  ('languish', 'definhar', 'To become weak or feeble; to lose strength or vitality.', 'The plant languished in the dark corner of the room.', 'C1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 48451),
  ('loath', 'relutante', 'Feeling strong aversion or unwillingness to do something, especially when it goes against one''s usual habits or preferences.', 'She was loath to leave her hometown after living there for decades.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48466),
  ('manganese', 'manganês', 'A hard, brittle, gray-white metal that resembles iron but is not magnetic. It is used in making steel and various alloys.', 'Manganese is essential for the production of high-strength steel.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 48477),
  ('pimento', 'pimento', 'A plant that produces large, mild, thick-walled fruits, often bell-shaped, commonly used in salads and cooking.', 'The pimento plant thrives in warm climates.', 'B1', 'noun', 'food', 48486),
  ('anemone', 'anêmone', 'A type of woodland plant from the genus Anemone, cultivated for its attractive flowers and distinctive whorls of finely divided leaves.', 'The garden was filled with white and pink anemones in early spring.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48502),
  ('apostolic', 'apostólico', 'Of or relating to the Apostles of Jesus Christ or their teachings and authority.', 'The apostolic tradition is central to many Christian denominations.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48504),
  ('miserly', 'pão-duro', 'Showing a complete lack of generosity; extremely reluctant to spend or share money.', 'He was so miserly that he never gave to charity.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48505),
  ('curare', 'curare', 'A toxic alkaloid found in certain tropical South American trees, used as a powerful relaxant for striated muscles.', 'Curare is used in medicine as a muscle relaxant during surgery.', 'C2', 'noun', 'science', 48515),
  ('usury', 'usura', 'An excessively high or illegal rate of interest charged on a loan.', 'The loan shark was convicted for charging usury.', 'C1', 'noun', 'law', 48523),
  ('pithy', 'sucinto', 'Brief but full of substance and meaning; expressing an idea in a few words.', 'The author''s pithy remarks made the article memorable.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48536),
  ('chamois', 'camurça', 'A soft, pliable suede leather, originally made from the skin of the chamois antelope but now typically made from sheepskin or other hides.', 'He polished his car with a chamois cloth.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48537),
  ('zoologist', 'zoólogo', 'A scientist who studies animals, their behavior, classification, and habitats.', 'The zoologist spent years studying the migration patterns of birds.', 'C2', 'noun', 'science', 48541),
  ('unconnected', 'desconectado', 'Describes things that are separate and not physically or logically attached.', 'The two pipes are unconnected and water cannot flow between them.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48560),
  ('ventriloquism', 'ventriloquia', 'The art of speaking in such a way that the voice appears to come from a source other than the speaker, such as a puppet or dummy.', 'He amazed the audience with his ventriloquism performance.', 'B2', 'noun', 'arts', 48586),
  ('capsize', 'soçobrar', 'To turn over or upset, especially a boat or ship in water.', 'The small boat capsized in the storm.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 48604),
  ('velvety', 'aveludado', 'Having a smooth, soft, and luxurious texture, like velvet fabric.', 'The velvety petals of the rose felt wonderful to the touch.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48620),
  ('anathema', 'anátema', 'Someone or something that is intensely disliked or loathed.', 'The idea of cheating is anathema to her.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48625),
  ('argent', 'prata', 'A precious metal, silver, often used in heraldry or poetic contexts.', 'The knight''s shield was emblazoned with a lion argent.', 'C2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48632),
  ('antagonism', 'antagonismo', 'A state of deep-seated dislike or opposition between people or groups.', 'There is a long history of antagonism between the two political parties.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48640),
  ('inexorably', 'inexoravelmente', 'In a manner that continues without possibility of being stopped or prevented.', 'The glacier moved inexorably down the valley.', 'C2', 'adverb', 'general-vocabulary', 48648),
  ('inconsistency', 'inconsistência', 'A situation where two or more statements or ideas cannot all be true at the same time.', 'There is an inconsistency in his testimony that the detective noticed.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48655),
  ('odorless', 'inodoro', 'Describes something that does not have any noticeable scent or odor.', 'The gas is odorless, so a special chemical is added to detect leaks.', 'B1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48656),
  ('hyperbole', 'hipérbole', 'Exaggerated statements or claims not meant to be taken literally, used for emphasis or dramatic effect.', 'The politician''s speech was full of hyperbole about the economy.', 'B2', 'noun', 'arts', 48664),
  ('bookseller', 'livreiro', 'A person who owns or manages a bookstore.', 'The bookseller recommended a new novel to me.', 'B1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48672),
  ('frighteningly', 'espantosamente', 'Used to emphasize that something is surprisingly or shockingly extreme.', 'The prices have risen frighteningly high.', 'B2', 'adverb', 'general-vocabulary', 48673),
  ('distancing', 'distanciamento', 'The act of keeping a certain amount of space between people or objects, often to prevent disease spread.', 'Social distancing became a common practice during the pandemic.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48693),
  ('samovar', 'samovar', 'A metal container, often ornately decorated, used in Russia and other Eastern European countries to heat water for making tea. It typically has a central tube for heating and a spigot at the bottom.', 'The family gathered around the samovar for afternoon tea.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48698),
  ('forfeiture', 'perda', 'The act of losing or being deprived of property, money, or rights as a penalty for a crime, breach of contract, or failure to fulfill an obligation.', 'The court ordered the forfeiture of all assets obtained through illegal activities.', 'C2', 'noun', 'law', 48701),
  ('grafting', 'enxerto', 'A method of plant propagation where tissues from one plant are joined to another so they grow together.', 'Grafting is commonly used to combine the best traits of two fruit trees.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 48708),
  ('personification', 'personificação', 'A person who is a perfect example of a particular quality or characteristic.', 'She is the personification of grace and elegance.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48711),
  ('constancy', 'constância', 'The quality of being faithful and reliable in relationships or commitments.', 'Her constancy in friendship is admired by everyone.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48712),
  ('acetylene', 'acetileno', 'A colorless, highly flammable gas (C2H2) used primarily in oxyacetylene welding and cutting, and in organic synthesis.', 'The welder used an acetylene torch to cut the steel beam.', 'C1', 'noun', 'science', 48714),
  ('liquidity', 'liquidez', 'The physical state of a substance that allows it to flow easily, with little tendency to disperse and relatively high incompressibility.', 'The liquidity of water decreases as it approaches freezing point.', 'B2', 'noun', 'business', 48721),
  ('palomino', 'palomino', 'A horse with a light tan or golden coat and a cream-colored or white mane and tail.', 'The palomino galloped gracefully across the field.', 'B1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48726),
  ('hypotenuse', 'hipotenusa', 'The side opposite the right angle in a right-angled triangle, which is the longest side.', 'In a right triangle, the hypotenuse is always the longest side.', 'B2', 'noun', 'technical', 48727),
  ('dengue', 'dengue', 'A viral infection transmitted by mosquitoes, common in tropical and subtropical regions, causing fever, severe headache, joint and muscle pain, and a rash.', 'Dengue is a major health concern in many tropical countries.', 'B2', 'noun', 'health', 48730),
  ('lubrication', 'lubrificação', 'The state of being made slippery or smooth through the use of a lubricating substance.', 'Proper lubrication reduces friction in the engine.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48736),
  ('unshakable', 'inabalável', 'Marked by firm determination or resolution; not easily moved or changed.', 'She has an unshakable belief in her own abilities.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48741),
  ('crumple', 'amassar', 'To press or crush something, such as paper or fabric, into irregular folds or wrinkles.', 'She crumpled the letter in anger and threw it away.', 'B1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 48747),
  ('stencil', 'estêncil', 'A thin sheet of material, such as metal, plastic, cardboard, or waxed paper, with a pattern cut out of it. Ink or paint is applied through the cut-out areas to reproduce the pattern on a surface below.', 'The artist used a stencil to spray-paint the logo onto the wall.', 'B1', 'noun', 'arts', 48766),
  ('copulate', 'copular', 'To have sex; to join in a sexual act, typically referring to animals or humans.', 'The pair of birds copulated during the mating season.', 'C1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 48794),
  ('parapet', 'parapeito', 'A low wall or railing built along the edge of a roof, balcony, bridge, or similar structure to prevent people from falling off.', 'She leaned over the parapet to look at the garden below.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48801),
  ('appropriation', 'apropriação', 'The deliberate act of taking or using something, often without the explicit consent of the owner.', 'The appropriation of indigenous cultural symbols by the fashion brand sparked controversy.', 'C1', 'noun', 'law', 48802),
  ('gyroscope', 'giroscópio', 'A device consisting of a spinning wheel or rotor that maintains its orientation regardless of the movement of its mount, used for navigation or stabilization.', 'The gyroscope in the aircraft helps maintain stable flight.', 'C1', 'noun', 'technical', 48814),
  ('rigidity', 'rigidez', 'The quality of being stiff, firm, and resistant to bending or deformation.', 'The rigidity of the steel beam ensures the bridge can support heavy loads.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48822),
  ('effusion', 'efusão', 'The escape of fluid into a body cavity or tissue, often due to injury or disease.', 'The patient was diagnosed with a pleural effusion.', 'C1', 'noun', 'health', 48824),
  ('basalt', 'basalto', 'A dense, dark grey, fine-grained volcanic rock formed from solidified lava, primarily composed of plagioclase feldspar and pyroxene.', 'The ocean floor is largely made of basalt.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 48844),
  ('gelding', 'capão', 'A male horse that has been castrated, typically used for riding or work.', 'The farmer bought a strong gelding for plowing the fields.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48854),
  ('osprey', 'águia-pesqueira', 'A large, long-winged hawk found worldwide that feeds primarily on fish and builds a large, bulky nest often reused for many years.', 'An osprey swooped down and caught a fish from the lake.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48858),
  ('calisthenics', 'calistenia', 'A form of exercise consisting of a variety of movements that use body weight for resistance to develop strength, flexibility, and endurance.', 'She does calisthenics every morning to stay fit.', 'B2', 'noun', 'sports', 48865),
  ('banality', 'banalidade', 'A statement that is unoriginal, dull, or lacking in freshness; a cliché.', 'His speech was full of banalities about the importance of teamwork.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48867),
  ('fifty-eight', 'cinquenta e oito', 'Being eight more than fifty in number.', 'There are fifty-eight students in the lecture hall.', 'A1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 48871),
  ('abstraction', 'abstração', 'A concept or idea that is not tied to any specific physical instance or concrete example.', 'Justice is an abstraction that can be difficult to define.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48877),
  ('gunboat', 'canhoneira', 'A small boat with a shallow draft that carries mounted guns, typically used for coastal patrol duties.', 'The navy deployed a gunboat to patrol the river delta.', 'B1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48882),
  ('ruination', 'ruína', 'An irrecoverable condition of complete destruction or decay.', 'The city fell into ruination after the war.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48888),
  ('dilate', 'expandir', 'To become wider, larger, or more open, especially in reference to a body part or opening.', 'The doctor used drops to dilate the patient''s pupils for the eye exam.', 'B2', 'verb', 'health', 48903),
  ('backhoe', 'retroescavadora', 'A piece of heavy equipment with a digging bucket attached to a hinged boom, used for excavating earth by drawing the bucket backward.', 'The construction crew used a backhoe to dig the foundation.', 'B2', 'noun', 'technical', 48933),
  ('animator', 'animador', 'A technician who produces animated cartoons or films by creating a sequence of images.', 'The animator spent months creating the characters for the movie.', 'B1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48936),
  ('turnstile', 'roleta', 'A mechanical gate with rotating arms that allows one person to pass through at a time, typically used to control entry or exit.', 'You need to insert your ticket into the turnstile to enter the subway.', 'B1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48950),
  ('ardor', 'ardor', 'A feeling of intense passion, excitement, or zeal for a cause, activity, or person.', 'She pursued her research with great ardor.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48951),
  ('mitigation', 'mitigação', 'The act of making an offense, problem, or negative situation seem less serious or severe.', 'The lawyer presented evidence in mitigation of his client''s actions.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 48985),
  ('inhibition', 'inibição', 'The conscious or unconscious exclusion of unacceptable thoughts, desires, or impulses.', 'His strict upbringing caused strong inhibitions about expressing anger.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 48991),
  ('optimization', 'otimização', 'The process of making something as good, effective, or functional as it can be.', 'The company focused on the optimization of its supply chain.', 'B2', 'noun', 'technical', 48995),
  ('parachuting', 'paraquedismo', 'The activity or sport of jumping from an aircraft and descending using a parachute.', 'Parachuting requires extensive training and safety checks.', 'B2', 'noun', 'sports', 48998),
  ('noteworthy', 'notável', 'Deserving to be noticed or observed because of being important or interesting.', 'The scientist made a noteworthy discovery about the planet''s atmosphere.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49008),
  ('vaccinate', 'vacinar', 'To give a vaccine to a person or animal in order to produce immunity against a disease.', 'The nurse vaccinated all the children against measles.', 'B1', 'verb', 'health', 49015),
  ('reverie', 'devaneio', 'A state of being pleasantly lost in one''s thoughts; a daydream.', 'She was lost in a reverie, staring out the window.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49028),
  ('subjugate', 'subjugar', 'To bring a person, group, or country under control, often by force.', 'The empire sought to subjugate the neighboring tribes.', 'C1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49035),
  ('ferrous', 'férreo', 'Relating to or containing iron, especially in its divalent form (Fe²⁺).', 'Ferrous metals are commonly used in construction due to their strength.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'technical', 49042),
  ('boffin', 'cientista', 'A person who is highly skilled or knowledgeable in a scientific or technical field, often involved in research and development.', 'The boffins at the lab developed a new type of battery.', 'C1', 'noun', 'science', 49047),
  ('bodywork', 'lataria', 'The outer shell or framework of a motor vehicle, including panels, doors, and roof.', 'The car''s bodywork was damaged in the accident.', 'B2', 'noun', 'technical', 49060),
  ('locus', 'sítio', 'The specific place where an event or action occurs, especially a meeting.', 'The park was the locus of the community gathering.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 49065),
  ('watermark', 'marca d''água', 'A line or mark indicating the height reached by a body of water, such as a river or tide.', 'The high watermark on the bridge showed the flood level.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49072),
  ('plantain', 'plantago', 'Any of numerous plants of the genus Plantago; mostly small roadside or dooryard weeds with elliptic leaves and small spikes of very small flowers; seeds of some used medicinally.', 'The common plantain grows easily in lawns and along paths.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 49080),
  ('cede', 'ceder', 'To formally give up control, possession, or rights to someone else, often after a conflict or negotiation.', 'The country was forced to cede territory after the war.', 'C1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49089),
  ('warble', 'gorjear', 'To sing or play a melody with a series of rapid, alternating pitches, often moving between a note and the half step above or below it.', 'The nightingale warbled its beautiful song in the garden.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49101),
  ('algonquin', 'algônquino', 'Of or pertaining to the Algonquin people, a group of Indigenous peoples in North America, primarily located in the subarctic regions of eastern Canada.', 'The Algonquin community has a rich tradition of storytelling.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49103),
  ('reticent', 'reticente', 'Inclined to be silent or uncommunicative; reserved in speech.', 'He was reticent about his past experiences.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49112),
  ('contortionist', 'contorcionista', 'An acrobat or performer who can twist their body into unusual and extreme positions.', 'The contortionist amazed the audience by bending backward and touching her head with her feet.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49114),
  ('suppository', 'supositório', 'A small, solid medication designed to be inserted into the rectum or vagina, where it dissolves or melts to release its active ingredients.', 'The doctor prescribed a suppository for the patient''s fever.', 'B2', 'noun', 'health', 49117),
  ('assent', 'assentimento', 'Official or formal agreement with a statement, proposal, or plan.', 'The board gave its assent to the new policy.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49122),
  ('franciscan', 'franciscano', 'Pertaining to Saint Francis of Assisi or the religious order he founded, the Franciscans, known for their commitment to poverty, humility, and service.', 'The Franciscan monastery was built in the 13th century.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49127),
  ('regress', 'regredir', 'To return to a former or less developed state, often in a negative sense.', 'The patient began to regress after stopping the medication.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49132),
  ('incalculable', 'incalculável', 'Too great or numerous to be counted or estimated.', 'The damage caused by the earthquake was incalculable.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49133),
  ('stratagem', 'estratagema', 'A carefully planned scheme or trick, especially for achieving a military advantage.', 'The general devised a clever stratagem to outflank the enemy.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49138),
  ('chopstick', 'hashi', 'One of a pair of thin, tapered sticks used as tableware, especially in East Asian cuisine, to pick up and eat food.', 'She used chopsticks to pick up the sushi.', 'A1', 'noun', 'food', 49141),
  ('gangplank', 'prancha', 'A movable bridge or ramp used to board or leave a ship or boat from a dock.', 'The passengers walked carefully across the gangplank to the ship.', 'B2', 'noun', 'technical', 49155),
  ('rebate', 'desconto', 'A partial refund or return of money paid for a product or service, often offered as an incentive.', 'The store offered a $50 rebate on the new smartphone.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49168),
  ('reintroduce', 'reintroduzir', 'To bring something back into use, existence, or practice after a period of absence.', 'The government plans to reintroduce the old tax law.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49184),
  ('spittle', 'cuspe', 'A clear liquid secreted into the mouth by the salivary glands and mucous glands; it moistens the mouth and begins the digestion of starches.', 'The baby drooled a bit of spittle onto his bib.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49189),
  ('countermeasure', 'contramedida', 'An action or strategy taken to counteract or neutralize the effects of another action or situation.', 'The government implemented new countermeasures to reduce pollution.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49190),
  ('aftershock', 'réplica', 'A smaller earthquake that follows the main shock of a seismic event, often causing additional damage.', 'The city experienced several aftershocks after the major earthquake.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 49199),
  ('coefficient', 'coeficiente', 'A constant number that multiplies a variable in an algebraic expression or equation.', 'In the equation 5x + 2y = 10, the coefficient of x is 5.', 'B2', 'noun', 'science', 49200),
  ('appraise', 'estimar', 'To assess the nature, quality, ability, extent, or significance of something.', 'The manager appraised the employee''s performance during the review.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49201),
  ('osteoporosis', 'osteoporose', 'A medical condition in which bones become weak, brittle, and more likely to break due to loss of bone density, often linked to calcium deficiency and common in older adults, especially postmenopausal women.', 'Osteoporosis increases the risk of hip fractures in elderly patients.', 'B2', 'noun', 'health', 49209),
  ('windward', 'barlavento', 'In the direction from which the wind is blowing; towards the source of the wind.', 'The ship sailed windward to avoid the storm.', 'C1', 'adverb', 'general-vocabulary', 49217),
  ('ectoplasm', 'ectoplasma', 'A mystical, viscous substance believed to emanate from a medium''s body during a spiritualist trance.', 'The medium claimed to produce ectoplasm during the séance.', 'C2', 'noun', 'science', 49226),
  ('cairn', 'moledro', 'A pile of stones, often conical, built as a memorial, landmark, or to mark a trail or boundary.', 'Hikers built a small cairn at the summit to mark the trail.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49227),
  ('unequivocal', 'inequívoco', 'Leaving no doubt; completely clear and certain.', 'The results of the experiment were unequivocal.', 'C2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49245),
  ('rutabaga', 'rutabaga', 'A large, round, yellow-fleshed root vegetable with a slightly sweet and earthy flavor, often used in cooking.', 'She mashed the rutabaga with butter and cream for a side dish.', 'B1', 'noun', 'food', 49253),
  ('hadron', 'hádron', 'Any elementary particle that interacts strongly with other particles, such as protons and neutrons.', 'Protons and neutrons are examples of hadrons.', 'C2', 'noun', 'science', 49270),
  ('assuage', 'acalmar', 'To make someone feel less angry, upset, or worried; to soothe or appease.', 'The manager tried to assuage the customer''s anger with a sincere apology.', 'C1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49283),
  ('obediently', 'obedientemente', 'In a way that follows orders, instructions, or rules without resistance.', 'The dog sat obediently by its owner''s side.', 'B2', 'adverb', 'general-vocabulary', 49284),
  ('writhe', 'retorcer-se', 'To make twisting or writhing movements, often due to pain, discomfort, or struggle.', 'The injured animal writhed in pain on the ground.', 'B2', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49292),
  ('sacrosanct', 'sacrossanto', 'Regarded as too important or valuable to be interfered with or criticized.', 'The principle of free speech is considered sacrosanct in many democracies.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49302),
  ('synchronicity', 'sincronicidade', 'The occurrence of events that seem meaningfully related but lack a causal connection, often considered significant.', 'He experienced a strange synchronicity when he thought of an old friend just before they called.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49308),
  ('inopportune', 'inoportuno', 'Happening at a time that is not suitable or convenient.', 'His arrival was inopportune, as we were just about to leave.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49316),
  ('beefsteak', 'bisteca', 'A thick slice of high-quality beef, typically cooked by broiling, grilling, or frying.', 'He ordered a rare beefsteak with a side of vegetables.', 'B1', 'noun', 'food', 49324),
  ('nanosecond', 'nanossegundo', 'One billionth (10^-9) of a second; one thousandth of a microsecond.', 'A nanosecond is a unit of time equal to one billionth of a second.', 'C1', 'noun', 'science', 49339),
  ('inexorable', 'inflexível', 'Continuing without possibility of being stopped; relentless.', 'The inexorable march of time cannot be reversed.', 'C2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49354),
  ('deft', 'hábil', 'Showing skill and quickness in movement or action.', 'The surgeon''s deft hands performed the delicate operation.', 'B2', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49359),
  ('paraphrase', 'paráfrase', 'A restatement of a passage or text using different words, often to clarify meaning.', 'The student wrote a paraphrase of the original poem.', 'B2', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49365),
  ('microcosm', 'microcosmo', 'A small, representative system that reflects the characteristics of a larger whole.', 'The classroom is a microcosm of society.', 'C1', 'noun', 'science', 49374),
  ('unblock', 'desbloquear', 'To clear or remove an obstruction from something, allowing it to function normally.', 'The plumber came to unblock the kitchen sink.', 'B1', 'verb', 'general-vocabulary', 49381),
  ('immutable', 'imutável', 'Not subject to change; constant and permanent.', 'The laws of physics are considered immutable.', 'C1', 'adjective', 'general-vocabulary', 49392),
  ('appeasement', 'apaziguamento', 'The act of satisfying or calming someone, often by giving in to their demands, especially in a political context.', 'The policy of appeasement towards the aggressor failed to prevent war.', 'C1', 'noun', 'general-vocabulary', 49396),
